## Results

| Run | Nonce | Scenario | Marker | Retired / stop | #PF / #GP | CPL0 RDTSC | CR3 changes | IRQ0 edges / delivered | Quanta | UART bytes / SHA-256 | Wall seconds |
|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|
| 0001 | `OD518e8717419d4b0e80000f36000000000` | failed | false | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 35 / 1 | 34,425,827 | 26,617 | 34,787 / 34,792 | 34,552,121 | 23,909 / `645ab37b020e2bd9d78de567c00f04d5ee160552cafb0c0855335d141e9eaeba` | 1,157.432 |
| 0002 | `OD518e87281985e2cd80000f36000000001` | passed | true | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 33 / 1 | 34,443,586 | 26,618 | 34,803 / 34,808 | 34,569,501 | 23,491 / `81f742f45148b8859f639e848f0b5fef2dfbdd2f0d0f7b1b3d7dc3379bdc39d9` | 1,163.126 |

Run 0001's exact marker line was merged with the kernel's
`Run /init as init process` printk:

```text
OD_NONCE=OD518e8717419d4b0e80000f36000000000[    2.271342] Run /init as init process
```

The strict marker validator rejected it. Run 0002 emitted its exact nonce line
and passed. Both guests loaded Linux and reached the expected budget stop.
Series outcome was `failed`; the command exited 1. The strict comparator reported
`matches=false` with unexplained `run[1].scenario_status`,
`run[1].marker_validation`, `run[1].machine_observations`, and
`run[1].ordered_uart_bytes`. The failed marker makes the Stage 4 nonce-variation
eligibility gate false, so its volatile-observation projection was not applied.
No comparator rule changed.

## Execution-observation sidecars

Each schema-v5 sidecar retained every delivered #PF and all CPL0 RDTSC site
counts: run 0001 has 35/35 #PF events and 22 sites; run 0002 has 33/33 #PF
events and 22 sites. Both report zero omitted #PF events, zero RDTSC site
overflow, and zero unattributed reads.

The CPL0 RDTSC total increased by 17,759 reads in run 0002. Eight of 22 sites
changed. The largest delta is 17,614 reads at RIP `0xffffffff8271b34d`
(`34,033,918` → `34,051,532`), which is 99.18% of the total delta. Other site
deltas (run 0002 minus run 0001) are: `0xffffffff813afa20` +64,
`0xffffffff8200796e` +36, `0xffffffff8271b31b` +18,
`0xffffffff8200713e` +16, `0xffffffff82726060` +15,
`0xffffffff8184f2f1` -2, and `0xffffffff81c02515` -2. The remaining 14 site
counts match. The same kernel debug ELF was previously used to resolve
`0xffffffff8271b34d` to `delay_tsc+0x4d`; `llvm-nm` also maps it to `delay_tsc`
at offset `+0x4d`. This localizes the largest count delta to the kernel delay
loop, but does not establish why its iteration count changed or classify the
observation as benign.

The first 30 ordered #PF signatures match. Run 0001 then has two extra CPL0
write faults; deleting those two records makes its remaining 33-record
sequence identical to run 0002:

| Run 0001 event | RIP / matched symbol | CR2 | Error | Original page walk |
|---:|---|---|---|---|
| 30 | `0xffffffff8271a9c1`, `rep_movs_alternative+0x11` | `0x7fffcfc42089` | `0x2`, write, CPL0 | `NotPresent { level: Pt }` |
| 31 | `0xffffffff8271ec4d`, `__put_user_8+0xd` | `0x7fffcfc41ed0` | `0x2`, write, CPL0 | `NotPresent { level: Pt }` |

The first RIP and the `delay_tsc` RIP were resolved against the matching
`vmlinux-debug` ELF. The per-event frame-chain and original page-walk records
are pre-delivery observations. They do not establish why the startup-stack
faults occur in one run and not the other, or prove the later PTE repair. The
RDTSC and #PF differences remain strict machine-observation differences.

